  "flow_summary": "The interviewer managed a challenging, disorganized patient with patience and persistence. While the interviewer successfully navigated the intake and handled the safety disclosure appropriately, the conversation was marred by frequent, repetitive loops during the PHQ-9 and GAD-7 sections, where the patient repeatedly lost the thread and the interviewer failed to adapt the delivery to be more accessible.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly re-asked the full PHQ-9 and GAD-7 questions verbatim when the patient expressed confusion, rather than simplifying the delivery or confirming understanding. For example: 'PHQ-9 Question 1: Over the last two weeks, how often have you had little interest or pleasure in doing things? 0 - Not at all 1 - Several days 2 - More than half the days 3 - Nearly every day' was repeated three times."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "In the personal history section, the interviewer struggled to recover from the patient's confusion, leading to a series of 'I don't know' responses that were not effectively probed or redirected: 'I’m not sure where you grew up. Could you name the city, town, or region?'"
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "The interviewer occasionally used slightly wordy or complex phrasing that contributed to the patient's confusion, such as: 'Apart from alcohol used as part of prescribed medical treatment—which is not applicable—have you ever used alcohol recreationally...'"
    }
